WEBVTT


00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.100
- Yes?
- Andrew Wyke?


00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.200
That's right.


00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.700
I'm Milo Tindle.


00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.700
Oh, yes, good.


00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.900
Glad to meet you.


00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.800
You got the train to Charlebury,
did you?


00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.300
- I drove.
- Oh, you drove?


00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.600
That's my car.


00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.700
Oh, the little one?


00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.600
- Not the big one.
- No, the big one's mine.


00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.700
What do you think of it?


00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.200
- Very handsome.
- Yeah.


00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.500
It is, isn't it?


00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.900
Come in.


00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.500
I was watching a video
of one of my books on television.


00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.700
Like the house?


00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.400
Extraordinary.


00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.300
You know who designed it,
who the interior decorator was?


00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.900
Yes, your wife.


00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.500
You knew?


00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.400
Yes, I knew.


00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.600
I'll show you around later.


00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:15.400
Have a drink. I'm drinking vodka.


00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.300
- Scotch, please.
- Scotch.


00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.900
Milo, what an interesting name.
You're a foreigner, I take it?


00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.600
My father's Italian.


00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.000
Milo sounds Hungarian.


00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.800
Does it?


00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.400
Here's your Scotch.


00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:35.700
Cheers.


00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.600
Cheers.


00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.400
You sure your father
isn't Hungarian?


00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.500
Well, if he is,
he's kept it a dead secret for years.


00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.300
- And your mother?
- English.


00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.900
So you're a kind of half-breed?


00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.000
Sit down.


00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.200
- Thanks for agreeing to see me.
- Not at all.


00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.500
I didn't know you wrote plays
for television.


00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.100
I don't. I write crime novels.
You must know that.


00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.300
I had heard.


00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.000
But sometimes they're adapted
for television by other people.


00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.400
You know what the word
adapted means, I take it?


00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.400
Adapted?


00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.600
They may not have such a word
in Italian.


00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.700
- I speak English.
- Good.


00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.300
Come and have a look
at my special book room.


00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.300
These are all my novels.


00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.500
You've read them, I suppose?


00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.500
Afraid not.


00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.700
Good God, no?
What about this one?


00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:47.100
- <i>Rat in a Trap?</i>
- No.


00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.900
- <i>The Obelisk?</i>
- No.


00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.100
- <i>Blackout?</i>
- No.


00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.800
- <i>Dead Fish?</i>
- Afraid not.


00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.900
God, you're one in a million.


00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.000
- Am I?
- Oh, absolu... I'm very popular.


00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.200
You see this shelf?


00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.400
Translations.


00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:07.000
French, Dutch, German.


00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.900
You speak Dutch yourself, do you?


00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.300
Yes, how did you know?
I have a Dutch uncle.


00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.400
Can't see any Italian translations.


00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:18.700
No, they're a funny lot, the Italians.
Culture isn't really their thing.


00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.300
Their salami's good, though.


00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.200
- Oh, is it?
- Italian salami? Best in the world.


00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.200
Did you bring any with you?


00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.500
- No, I left it at home.
- Oh, shame.


00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.400
We're gonna have it
for supper tonight.


00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.500
With a couple of bottles
of Valpolicella.


00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.600
- We?
- Maggie and me.


00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:38.700
Your glass is empty.
What were you drinking, vodka?


00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.400
- Scotch.
- Scotch.


00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.400
<i>I want to come to the point.</i>


00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:56.900
<i>Point? What point?</i>


00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:59.000
<i>Are you gonna give Maggie</i>
<i>a divorce?</i>


00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:00.500
<i>And if not, why not?</i>


00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.100
<i>Yeah, yes, yes, we'll come to that.</i>


00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.200
<i>She thinks</i>
<i>you're being unreasonable.</i>


00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.000
<i>So do I.</i>


00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.400
<i>She's never coming back to you,</i>
<i>so why not just give her the divorce?</i>


00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.900
<i>It'll do her good to wait for five years.</i>
<i>Good for her character.</i>


00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.600
<i>You're going to make her wait</i>
<i>five years?</i>


00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.300
- <i>That's the law. The law of the land.</i>
- <i>But that's pure spite.</i>


00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:24.700
<i>Anyway, we'll get back to that,</i>
<i>perhaps. Have your drink first.</i>


00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.400
<i>What do you do, by the way?</i>


00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.100
<i>I'm an actor.</i>


00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.700
<i>Good God. Are you really?</i>


00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.700
<i>I thought Maggie said</i>
<i>you were a hairdresser.</i>


00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.000
<i>She must have been talking</i>
<i>about someone else.</i>


00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.600
<i>You mean another friend?</i>


00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.300
<i>Another friend?</i>


00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.200
<i>She tends to have</i>
<i>more than one friend.</i>


00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.600
- <i>Does she?</i>
- <i>Oh, yes.</i>


00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:48.200
<i>I'm her only friend.</i>


00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.900
<i>She must be lonely.</i>


00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.700
<i>She's not.</i>


00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.600
<i>Acting is a pretty precarious</i>
<i>profession, isn't it?</i>


00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.000
<i>What are you acting in</i>
<i>at the moment?</i>


00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.100
<i>I'm out of work.</i>


00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.300
<i>Poor chap.</i>


00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.200
<i>I drive cars now and again,</i>
<i>chauffeuring.</i>


00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.800
- <i>Oh, tough life.</i>
- <i>I keep my head above water.</i>


00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.500
<i>What sort of parts do you play?</i>


00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.900
Killers, mostly.


00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.100
Sex maniacs, perverts.


00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.900
But you're so charming.


00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.700
Yes, I know.
Anyway, what about this divorce?


00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:24.100
What's your position, exactly?


00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.700
All in good time.


00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.200
Come in.


00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.300
Have a seat.
Make yourself comfortable.


00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.800
I understand you're fucking my wife.


00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:58.100
- That's right.
- Right.


00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.900
Yes, right.


00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:02.200
- So we've cleared that up.
- We have.


00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.600
- I thought you might deny it.
- Why would I deny it?


00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.600
- Well, she is my wife.
- Yes, but she's fucking me.


00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.500
Oh, she's fucking you too?
Well, I'll be buggered.


00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.000
- Sorry.
- Yes, it's mutual.


00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:14.900
- You take turns?
- We fuck each other.


00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:19.000
- That's what people do.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. I follow.


00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.500
- We're in love.
- You're in love?


00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.100
That's right.


00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.900
Let me top you up.


00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:43.600
I heard a rumor
that you wanted to marry her.


00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.700
- That can't be true, can it?
- Why not?


00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.800
In this day and age,
is marriage absolutely necessary?


00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Isn't it a bit old hat?


00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.100
- Is it?
- It's a mug's game.


00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.900
I wouldn't go near it if I were you.
You can't marry her.


00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.200
You can't marry her
because she's married to me.


00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:59.100
Unless I divorce her, of course.


00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.300
- And are you?
- Am I what?


00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.600
Going to divorce her?


00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.800
Are you really gonna
make her wait five years?


00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.900
- She wants to know.
- To be honest, I can't wait.


00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.300
But there are one or two things
I'd like to clear up first.


00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:16.100
For example, I've never heard
of an Italian called Tindle.


00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.800
My father's name is Tindolini.


00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:21.300
Now, that's lovely.
That's like a little bell.


00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:24.400
Why don't you go back to Tindolini?
It suits you.


00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.100
- You think so?
- Yes.


00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:30.900
So if and when you marry Maggie,
she'll be Maggie Tindolini.


00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.500
Do you get a kick out of that?


00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.500
What name do you act under?
Tindle or Tindolini?


00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.600
- Tindle.
- Why have I never heard of you?


00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.100
You will before long.


00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.200
- Really?
- In spades.


00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:44.000
- That sounds threatening.
- Does it?


00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.600
Doesn't it?


00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.300
Why don't we get down
to brass tacks?


00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.400
Brass tacks, yes. Why not?


00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:58.000
This is the way I see it.


00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:00.700
Come upstairs.


00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.700
I want to show you something.


00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.800
Are you all right in elevators?


00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.900
It won't make you sick
or anything, will it?


00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.000
This is our bedroom.


00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:42.300
And this is my wife's dressing room.


00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.800
She left a few dresses.
Couldn't be bothered to pick them up.


00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:50.300
They're worth thousands.
Thousands.


00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.100
This leather coat alone
is worth 5000 quid.


00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.900
So you see, the thing is this.
Sit down.


00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.700
The thing is this,
my wife spends money like water.


00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:08.200
So if you're not careful,
she'll eat you out of house and home.


00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.600
She was born to luxury, you know.
Jamaica, the Ritz, the Swiss Alps.


00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:15.600
What are you?
Out-of-work actor, part-time chauffeur.


00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.800
You're out of your depth, old boy.
You're on a hiding to nothing.


00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:20.600
If you think you're broke now...


00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.000
...you'll be 10 times broker
by the time she's finished with you.


00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:26.000
She'll have your guts for garters.


00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.500
- She's in love with me.
- Oh, never trust in love, chum.


00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:33.700
Love will kick you up the arse
as soon as look at you.


00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:37.400
One minute, it's love,
10 minutes later, it's contempt.


00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.200
That's your own experience, is it?


00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:42.200
Oh, no, no, no, that's observation.


00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.600
Don't forget, I'm a novelist.


00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.300
I observe people.


00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.100
What I'm getting at is you won't
be able to give her what she wants.


00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:54.100
So she's gonna leave you,
come back to me.


00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:56.900
I don't want her near me.
That's the last thing I want.


00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.900
I've had her up to here.


00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.200
Anyway, I've got this lovely mistress.
She runs a sauna in Swindon.


00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.500
She's my girl.


00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.600
So you see,
I want Maggie to stay with you.


00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:10.700
I want you two
to be together forever.


00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.200
But unless you listen to me...


00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:14.600
...the whole thing
will be a fucking disaster...


00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:18.300
...with catastrophic consequences
all round.


00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:23.800
But I have a solution.


00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.800
You won't believe
what I'm gonna say.


00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:34.800
What are you gonna say?


00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.500
I'm all ears.


00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.100
You know something?


00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.200
I'm beginning to respond
to your charm.


00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.900
- Get away.
- No, it's true.


00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:46.500
- I'm really touched.
- You should be.


00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:50.000
Tell me, I bet you didn't expect me
to be so intelligent.


00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.100
So quick-witted, did you?


00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:54.400
Oh, I did.


00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.500
Quite.


00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.300
Maggie told you, did she?


00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.700
What's your solution?


00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.300
It's a close fit, isn't it?


00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.300
For two.


00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:26.200
Listen, I'm going
to make you a proposition.


00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:29.700
A few years ago,
I gave her some jewels.


00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:32.200
Amazingly expensive.


00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:36.300
I didn't give them to her, I own them.
They're insured in my name.


00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:39.800
But I let her use them
on special occasions.


00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.800
They're worth 1 million pounds.


00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:46.200
They spend half the time in the bank,
half the time in the safe.


00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:51.300
At the moment, they're here
in the house, in the safe.


00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:55.500
And I want you to steal them.


00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.300
- Steal them?
- That's right.


00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:06.000
- What the hell do you mean?
- I want you to steal the jewels.


00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.600
You want me to steal the jewels?
I don't get it.


00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:11.500
It's simple. You steal the jewels,
sell them abroad...


00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:14.400
...and you live happily ever after
with Maggie.


00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.100
I get rid of my wife
and I'll be like a pig in shit.


00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:20.700
You can keep Maggie in the manner
to which she's become accustomed.


00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:24.100
You want me to take part
in a scummy little plot...


00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.600
...to defraud your insurance company,
is that it?


00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.300
I thought it was quite elegant.


00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.000
What do you think I am?


00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.800
What the fuck
are you actually talking about?


00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.400
- These are real facts.
- This is a joke.


00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.600
- No.
- It's also a trap.


00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:38.400
- A trap?
- Yes. You think I'm a fool.


00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.800
Well, are you?


00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.300
- It doesn't hold up.
- Why not?


00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.000
They're worth a million pounds. You'd
get a fraction of that from any fence.


00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.300
I have already contacted
a friend of mine in Amsterdam.


00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:54.000
And he will give you
800,000 pounds tax-free.


00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.200
Now, think about it.


00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.000
Eight hundred thousand pounds...


00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.300
...tax-free.


00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.200
Why would he do that?


00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:08.100
When you steal the jewels,
you will also steal the receipts.


00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:12.000
So he'll have title to the jewels
as well as the jewels themselves...


00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.800
...so that when he sells them,
he gets full value.


00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.100
Got it?


00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.000
Think about it.


00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.300
Take your time.


00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.200
And why would you do all this?


00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:50.100
Listen, under this crooked exterior,
I am a simple, honest man.


00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.900
Every word I've told you is true,
I swear it.


00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:59.500
I want to get rid of my wife,
but I want it to be solid, permanent.


00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:02.700
I don't want her on my back.
I want her to stay on your back.


00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.400
This is a frame-up.


00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.900
- A frame-up?
- Yes.


00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.700
You want to destroy me.


00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:11.100
You want to see me in jail.


00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:14.800
You want me to do this
and then shop me to the police.


00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.200
No, no, no.


00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:20.700
If I shop you, then you'll shop me,
and then we'll both end up in jail.


00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.300
No, I take a strictly moral position
on all this.


00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.500
My wife is an adulteress.


00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:28.000
Actually,
she should be stoned to death.


00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:30.900
Anyway, it's up to you.
Make up your own mind.


00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:32.500
You're asking me to trust you?


00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:34.600
I don't give a fuck
if you trust me or not.


00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.400
This is a simple proposition.


00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.200
You have an expensive woman
and no money.


00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:42.400
You wanna keep the woman,
steal the jewels.


