00:53:09.800 --> 00:53:12.200
Where's the body?
What have you done with the body?


00:53:12.400 --> 00:53:13.400
There's no body.


00:53:13.600 --> 00:53:15.600
Don't fuck about!


00:53:15.800 --> 00:53:17.600
Don't bullshit me.
I won't stand for it.


00:53:17.800 --> 00:53:19.900
Where is it?
In the house or did you shift it?


00:53:20.100 --> 00:53:22.100
There is no body!


00:53:30.700 --> 00:53:33.800
Here, look at this.
You got holes in your walls.


00:53:36.700 --> 00:53:39.700
They're bullet holes.
Live bullet holes.


00:53:39.800 --> 00:53:42.000
I fired two live bullets
to set up the trick...


00:53:42.100 --> 00:53:43.700
...and one blank to complete it.


00:53:43.900 --> 00:53:46.400
It was a game, I told you.
I played it to the hilt.


00:53:46.600 --> 00:53:49.300
It's not worth playing
unless you play it to the hilt.


00:53:49.500 --> 00:53:51.700
- The third shot was a blank?
- That's right.


00:53:51.900 --> 00:53:52.900
- What's that?
- What?


00:53:53.100 --> 00:53:55.100
Blood. Dried blood!


00:53:55.300 --> 00:53:57.600
Some of it's not even dried.
It's still damp.


00:53:57.700 --> 00:53:59.600
- That's impossible.
- That's blood, chum.


00:53:59.800 --> 00:54:01.700
- Whose blood is it?
- It's impossible.


00:54:01.900 --> 00:54:03.400
It was a game. It was a blank.


00:54:03.600 --> 00:54:06.000
No, it was a game
with real bullets and real blood.


00:54:06.200 --> 00:54:07.500
This is a carve-up.


00:54:07.700 --> 00:54:11.500
Let's see what else
is new around here.


00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:13.900
Hello, what's this?


00:54:14.700 --> 00:54:18.700
We've got a shirt, jacket and trousers
in the back of your cupboard.


00:54:18.900 --> 00:54:21.700
Very negligent of you, mate,
unless they're not yours.


00:54:21.900 --> 00:54:25.800
No, I don't think they're yours.
I think they belong to Tindle.


00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:28.800
You say he left the house
after you shot him.


00:54:28.900 --> 00:54:30.800
- Yes.
- Naked?


00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:32.500
I don't know how those got there.


00:54:32.600 --> 00:54:35.000
So you made him strip
before you shot him?


00:54:35.200 --> 00:54:37.200
Part of the humiliation, was it?


00:54:37.400 --> 00:54:38.900
No. The thing is this.


00:54:39.100 --> 00:54:42.100
It might have started as a game,
but it got out of hand.


00:54:42.300 --> 00:54:44.600
The third shot was live!


00:54:44.800 --> 00:54:48.200
It killed him. So where's the body?


00:54:48.400 --> 00:54:50.500
I didn't kill him! He's alive!


00:54:50.700 --> 00:54:52.800
Bollocks. You're a joker, all right.


00:54:53.000 --> 00:54:54.500
A real joker.


00:54:54.700 --> 00:54:56.500
Come on, we're off to the station.


00:54:56.700 --> 00:54:59.300
- There's something very wrong here.
- Hey, dead right.


00:54:59.500 --> 00:55:02.800
I'll tell you what you are.
You're fucked.


00:55:03.200 --> 00:55:04.300
Jesus Christ.


00:55:04.400 --> 00:55:06.700
Don't struggle, chum.
I'll have you for breakfast.


00:55:06.900 --> 00:55:08.200
There's something wrong here.


00:55:08.400 --> 00:55:12.300
You're up shit creek, Wyke.
You're up shit creek without a paddle.


00:55:15.700 --> 00:55:19.200
Look at you. All aquiver.


00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:22.100
Who's the dead duck?


00:55:25.900 --> 00:55:27.300
Jesus Christ.


00:55:30.900 --> 00:55:34.600
You're the dead duck.


00:55:37.300 --> 00:55:43.100
I just sucked you in
and blew you out in little bubbles.


00:55:43.300 --> 00:55:44.800
- It's you.
- It's me, all right.


00:55:44.900 --> 00:55:47.300
You bastard. You stinking bastard.


00:55:47.500 --> 00:55:48.900
Just a little game, Andrew.


00:55:49.000 --> 00:55:51.000
- Just a little game.
- You shit.


00:55:51.200 --> 00:55:53.900
- I thought it might amuse you.
- You're a total shit.


00:55:54.100 --> 00:55:55.400
I know I am.


00:55:55.600 --> 00:55:59.200
- But you're also a genius.
- I know that too.


00:56:01.700 --> 00:56:04.000
When did you do this?
The clothes in the wardrobe?


00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:06.800
- The blood?
- The blood belongs to a pig's liver.


00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:09.200
But when did you do it?
How did you do it?


00:56:09.300 --> 00:56:12.300
I did it last night. I used that ladder.
I heard you snoring.


00:56:12.500 --> 00:56:15.600
Does Maggie know about this?
Your detective, was it her idea?


00:56:15.700 --> 00:56:18.200
- How much does she know?
- She knows nothing about it.


00:56:18.300 --> 00:56:21.500
Entirely my own idea.


00:56:21.600 --> 00:56:24.600
This is a game between us, old boy.


00:56:24.800 --> 00:56:27.700
Between you and me.


00:56:27.800 --> 00:56:30.300
Don't forget, I'm half Italian.


00:56:30.500 --> 00:56:32.100
We go in for revenge.


00:56:45.100 --> 00:56:49.500
After all, you frightened
the life out of me deliberately.


00:56:49.700 --> 00:56:52.500
You fired two live bullets
into the wall...


00:56:52.700 --> 00:56:56.400
...and then you pointed
the gun at me.


00:56:56.600 --> 00:56:58.800
And then you fired.


00:57:02.600 --> 00:57:04.300
I don't like guns.


00:57:05.600 --> 00:57:07.300
They kill you.


00:57:10.600 --> 00:57:12.300
Okay.


00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:14.900
So, what does this make the score?


00:57:16.000 --> 00:57:18.000
You've had your revenge.


00:57:18.200 --> 00:57:22.400
So, what do you reckon?


00:57:22.900 --> 00:57:24.800
One set all?


00:57:25.300 --> 00:57:27.700
No, no, you're way ahead.


00:57:28.500 --> 00:57:32.800
I only teased you with my inspector,
gave you a few goose pimples.


00:57:33.800 --> 00:57:35.400
But you frightened me to death.


00:57:37.600 --> 00:57:40.200
Did you really think
I was going to kill you?


00:57:40.400 --> 00:57:44.000
You fainted, you see.
It was a blank.


00:57:45.100 --> 00:57:48.300
I may be three games up
in the second set.


00:57:48.400 --> 00:57:49.500
If I had killed you...


00:57:49.600 --> 00:57:53.000
...I'd have to bury the body
in the garden or somewhere.


00:57:53.100 --> 00:57:54.200
Too exhausting.


00:57:54.300 --> 00:57:55.800
But you won the first, 6-Iove.


00:58:00.500 --> 00:58:03.000
So we're a long way
from one set all.


00:58:09.700 --> 00:58:12.700
By the way, I spoke to Maggie.


00:58:12.900 --> 00:58:15.800
I told her all about you.


00:58:16.000 --> 00:58:17.500
She loved it.


00:58:18.600 --> 00:58:19.800
Loved what?


00:58:20.300 --> 00:58:23.100
That I frightened the life out of you.


00:58:23.200 --> 00:58:24.600
That you pissed your pants.


00:58:26.600 --> 00:58:29.100
And that you actually fainted.


00:58:29.200 --> 00:58:32.200
She said to me,
"You mean he actually fainted?"


00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:35.100
I said, "Dead out,
he was scared shitless.


00:58:36.600 --> 00:58:38.100
Went out like a light."


00:58:39.600 --> 00:58:43.700
She laughed so much,
I thought she was gonna burst.


00:58:48.200 --> 00:58:52.100
Oh, incidentally,
she's coming back to me.


00:58:52.800 --> 00:58:54.100
Oh, is she?


00:58:54.300 --> 00:58:56.000
Yes, that's right.


00:58:56.200 --> 00:58:58.000
You know what she said about you?


00:58:58.100 --> 00:58:59.200
What?


00:58:59.400 --> 00:59:00.700
She said:


00:59:00.800 --> 00:59:04.200
"Faint heart never won fair lady."


00:59:06.700 --> 00:59:07.900
Is that a fact?


00:59:08.000 --> 00:59:09.300
Yeah.


00:59:11.200 --> 00:59:15.400
Listen, I want to
show you something.


00:59:15.800 --> 00:59:19.100
Go into your study and sit down.


00:59:21.400 --> 00:59:22.900
Go into my study?


00:59:24.400 --> 00:59:26.600
And sit down.


00:59:30.100 --> 00:59:33.100
- What are you doing?
- It's late at night.


00:59:33.300 --> 00:59:35.600
You're reading a book under a lamp.
Read something.


00:59:35.800 --> 00:59:38.300
- What's going on?
- Read a book.


00:59:38.500 --> 00:59:40.900
It's late at night.
You're reading a book.


00:59:41.100 --> 00:59:43.200
You hear something. You look up.


00:59:43.300 --> 00:59:45.100
It's me jumping off the ladder.


00:59:45.300 --> 00:59:46.900
You see me with this gun.


00:59:47.100 --> 00:59:51.100
You're caught like a rat in a trap.
You stare at the gun, you're paralyzed.


00:59:51.300 --> 00:59:52.600
I've come for the jewels.


00:59:52.800 --> 00:59:54.500
- Where is the safe?
- What jewels?


00:59:54.700 --> 00:59:56.100
The jewels. Where's the safe?


00:59:56.300 --> 00:59:57.700
- You know where it is.
- I don't.


00:59:57.900 --> 01:00:00.000
- You don't?
- Don't fuck me about, I mean it.


01:00:00.200 --> 01:00:01.700
Get up.


01:00:02.500 --> 01:00:04.900
You think this gun isn't real?


01:00:07.600 --> 01:00:09.500
Where is it?


01:00:10.200 --> 01:00:13.200
- Upstairs.
- Well, let's go upstairs.


01:00:13.900 --> 01:00:19.200
Get up these stairs
or I'll ram this gun right up your ass.


01:00:19.400 --> 01:00:22.700
- The safe is behind the fish tank.
- How am I gonna get to it?


01:00:22.800 --> 01:00:25.500
Well, you press the button
and the button moves the tank.


01:00:25.700 --> 01:00:27.900
Then press it.


01:00:28.100 --> 01:00:30.600
It's not working. It's out of ord...


01:00:32.100 --> 01:00:33.500
Are you a maniac? You're crazy.


01:00:33.700 --> 01:00:36.400
- Open it.
- I changed the combination yesterday.


01:00:36.600 --> 01:00:39.100
- What is it?
- I forgot. I can't remember.


01:00:39.300 --> 01:00:41.300
- Remember.
- It's the truth. I can't remember.


01:00:41.500 --> 01:00:42.600
Remember!


01:00:45.700 --> 01:00:47.600
What are you doing?
What are you gonna do?


01:00:47.700 --> 01:00:51.900
I've broken into your house because
I know you have jewels in a safe.


01:00:52.700 --> 01:00:55.400
I have inside information.
I want them.


01:00:55.600 --> 01:00:58.000
Remember the combination
and open it.


01:01:05.200 --> 01:01:07.200
It was a blank.


01:01:08.800 --> 01:01:10.300
The next one's real.


01:01:28.800 --> 01:01:30.600
There's a good boy.


01:01:48.700 --> 01:01:51.200
So, what are you writing
at the moment?


01:01:56.100 --> 01:01:57.800
What am I writing?


01:01:58.300 --> 01:02:00.300
Yes, I'm very interested in literature.


01:02:04.800 --> 01:02:07.500
Do you mind if I have a drink?


01:02:07.700 --> 01:02:11.300
Sure. It's your house.


01:02:11.700 --> 01:02:15.900
I'm always interested
in the people I rob.


01:02:16.100 --> 01:02:20.100
Like I'm always interested
in the husbands of the wives I fuck.


01:02:21.700 --> 01:02:23.400
Are you really?


01:02:24.100 --> 01:02:25.800
Well, well.


01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:28.600
Cheers.


01:02:35.100 --> 01:02:39.600
So, what are you writing?


01:02:44.400 --> 01:02:48.100
It's the story of a pathological killer.


01:02:48.200 --> 01:02:51.300
- I call it <i>The Smiling Man.</i>
- Does he come to a bad end?


01:02:51.500 --> 01:02:54.400
He dies during the act of love.
Like countless others.


01:02:54.600 --> 01:02:55.800
Countless others, eh?


01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:58.400
I can see you've researched
the subject thoroughly.


01:02:59.500 --> 01:03:02.900
- What subject?
- Death in orgasm.


01:03:03.000 --> 01:03:06.800
Isn't that a beautiful notion?
To die in the arms of your beloved.


01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:10.700
Can you imagine
anything more poignant?


01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:13.000
- I can't, no.
- No.


01:03:13.200 --> 01:03:17.600
- You're a married man, aren't you?
- Yeah, been married 13 years.


01:03:17.700 --> 01:03:19.000
It was love at first sight.


01:03:19.200 --> 01:03:20.500
- Very moving.
- Yeah.


01:03:20.700 --> 01:03:22.900
And we're still in love.
Like two peas in a pod.


01:03:23.100 --> 01:03:25.700
Someone told me
your wife has a lover.


01:03:25.800 --> 01:03:27.900
- She has, yeah.
- Do you know him?


01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:30.900
No, I've never met him.
He's some sort of Italian.


01:03:31.100 --> 01:03:33.400
Called Tandoori or something.


01:03:33.600 --> 01:03:35.600
One of the Bombay Tandooris?


01:03:35.800 --> 01:03:37.800
You've got it, yeah.


01:03:37.900 --> 01:03:40.800
You know something? I've never met
an artistic burglar before.


01:03:41.000 --> 01:03:43.100
That's fantastic.


01:03:44.300 --> 01:03:46.200
- What's your background?
- Me?


01:03:46.400 --> 01:03:48.800
- You.
- Irish. Connemara.


01:03:49.000 --> 01:03:51.200
Spanish descent.
By way of Uganda.


01:03:51.400 --> 01:03:53.100
My grandparents were slaves.


01:03:53.200 --> 01:03:56.300
My mother was a dark-eyed,
dusky beauty.


01:03:56.400 --> 01:04:00.100
- Were you breastfed?
- Oh, sure, like a baby.


01:04:01.700 --> 01:04:07.400
Shall I tell you what I want you to do
with these jewels?


01:04:08.300 --> 01:04:09.800
What?


01:04:22.200 --> 01:04:27.500
You look so charming.


01:04:33.900 --> 01:04:35.500
How do you want it?


01:04:35.600 --> 01:04:37.200
Like this?


01:04:37.400 --> 01:04:39.800
Or shorter?


01:04:40.800 --> 01:04:45.100
How about this?
Or even shorter like a halter?


01:04:45.300 --> 01:04:48.800
- You're hurting me.
- Oh, am I hurting you?


01:04:48.900 --> 01:04:52.600
- Yes. Don't hurt me.
- Are you sensitive to pain?


01:04:52.800 --> 01:04:55.000
Very. Very.


01:04:55.200 --> 01:04:57.700
I wouldn't want to hurt you,
sweetheart.


01:04:57.900 --> 01:05:00.400
You're too much fun.


01:05:00.600 --> 01:05:04.400
- Am I really?
- Oh, yes. You're wicked.


01:05:04.600 --> 01:05:07.500
I like that. Yeah.


01:05:08.700 --> 01:05:10.700
Do you know something?


01:05:11.900 --> 01:05:15.000
I don't think
these earrings really suit me.


01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:20.100
You're right. Take them off.


01:05:24.100 --> 01:05:25.800
I don't...


01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:30.600
I don't think this bracelet
is really my style either.


01:05:32.500 --> 01:05:34.900
But the necklace is nice.


01:05:36.300 --> 01:05:37.500
I'm not totally sure.


01:05:37.600 --> 01:05:42.500
Listen, you can play with these jewels
until the cows come home.


01:05:42.700 --> 01:05:47.200
They're yours.
Do what you like with them.


01:05:49.800 --> 01:05:52.900
But I thought you'd just stolen them.


01:05:53.100 --> 01:05:55.500
No, no! It was a game!


01:05:55.700 --> 01:06:00.700
It was just a game!
I thought it might amuse you.


01:06:17.900 --> 01:06:19.400
Well...


01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:24.600
Aren't you the wicked one?


01:06:32.100 --> 01:06:33.300
You remember what I said?


01:06:35.000 --> 01:06:38.400
You won the first set, 6-Iove.
I was 3-Iove up in the second.


01:06:38.600 --> 01:06:43.000
Well, now it's one set all.


01:06:53.100 --> 01:06:56.700
But who's going to win the third set?


01:06:58.900 --> 01:07:01.000
Remains to be seen.


01:07:19.900 --> 01:07:21.300
You like games, don't you?


01:07:22.600 --> 01:07:25.000
Some. Not all.


01:07:25.200 --> 01:07:27.700
But you like being in charge...


01:07:27.900 --> 01:07:29.700
...of the game?


01:07:31.000 --> 01:07:33.400
Oh, yes. Sure.


01:07:35.100 --> 01:07:38.100
I like a man who wants
to be in charge of things.


01:07:38.300 --> 01:07:41.000
- Do you?
- Yes, I do.


01:07:42.400 --> 01:07:44.500
Listen, you've met my wife, I think.


01:07:45.900 --> 01:07:49.700
I have met her. Yes.


01:07:49.900 --> 01:07:52.800
- Did she say if she had a husband?
- Yes.


01:07:52.900 --> 01:07:55.600
Yeah, she said she had a husband.


01:07:56.400 --> 01:07:59.000
How did she describe him?


01:08:01.000 --> 01:08:03.400
Remote. Cold.


01:08:03.600 --> 01:08:06.500
Malevolent. Spiteful.


01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:09.600
Arrogant. Ruthless.


01:08:09.800 --> 01:08:11.600
Jealous. Paranoid.


01:08:11.800 --> 01:08:15.700
Criminal tendencies.
Mentally unsound.


01:08:15.900 --> 01:08:17.300
That's me, all right.


01:08:21.700 --> 01:08:24.100
You know something?
I like your mind.


01:08:24.800 --> 01:08:26.900
- Do you really?
- It excites me.


01:08:27.300 --> 01:08:29.200
I like the way you go about things.


01:08:31.000 --> 01:08:34.300
You mean you like my style?


01:08:34.500 --> 01:08:36.700
Oh, I like your style.


01:08:36.900 --> 01:08:39.400
I like it very much.


01:08:40.500 --> 01:08:44.200
Look, I want to
make you a proposition.


01:08:45.200 --> 01:08:46.700
What?


01:08:49.000 --> 01:08:51.100
I want to show you something.


01:08:55.400 --> 01:08:59.200
- Can't you put that gun down now?
- No.


01:08:59.300 --> 01:09:02.500
God, you're so strong, so ruthless,
aren't you?


01:09:02.600 --> 01:09:03.700
Yes.


01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:06.600
Have you any idea
what my proposition is going to be?


01:09:06.800 --> 01:09:09.100
- No.
- Are you excited?


01:09:09.300 --> 01:09:10.400
I'd say intrigued.


01:09:10.600 --> 01:09:13.300
I think you're going to be excited
very much.


01:09:13.500 --> 01:09:16.900
This is the guest suite.


01:09:18.600 --> 01:09:22.000
Isn't it nice? Look at the view.


01:09:23.000 --> 01:09:25.100
There's a private bathroom.
A small fridge.


01:09:25.300 --> 01:09:30.500
A bottle of Chilean Chardonnay
is chilling in there at this very moment.


01:09:31.900 --> 01:09:34.700
This suite is uninhabited.


01:09:36.200 --> 01:09:37.800
It has no occupant.


01:09:43.500 --> 01:09:45.300
How would you like it?


01:09:48.700 --> 01:09:50.000
Me?


01:09:52.300 --> 01:09:53.700
Yes, yes.


01:09:53.900 --> 01:09:58.700
I think I've come to the conclusion
that you're my kind of person.


01:10:01.700 --> 01:10:03.200
Am I, now?


01:10:03.800 --> 01:10:06.400
Well, I told you.
I liked your mind. It excited me.


01:10:06.500 --> 01:10:10.400
I need intellectual excitement.


01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:12.900
Intellectual stimulation.


01:10:14.900 --> 01:10:16.800
Well, they don't grow on trees.


01:10:17.500 --> 01:10:19.800
I'm a rich man.


01:10:20.000 --> 01:10:22.000
What do you want to do?


01:10:22.200 --> 01:10:24.800
I can subsidize anything you want.


01:10:25.900 --> 01:10:28.600
You want to open a bookshop
in the village?


01:10:29.400 --> 01:10:33.000
An art gallery?
Or, of course, a little theater.


01:10:33.500 --> 01:10:34.600
You're a wonderful actor.


01:10:34.800 --> 01:10:38.800
You could choose all the plays
and play all the leading parts.


01:10:40.300 --> 01:10:44.600
But this would be your home.


01:10:49.200 --> 01:10:51.900
And this would be your bedroom.


01:10:56.900 --> 01:11:00.100
You're asking me to live here?


01:11:01.900 --> 01:11:05.300
Yes, I'm asking you to stay with me.


01:11:06.000 --> 01:11:10.300
Oh, we would also travel.
